<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!-- Anonymization tool, complete package for a STANDARD TEKCO org.

     WHAT IT DEPLOYS: every piece of anonymization metadata in this repository except the
     TEKCO_AnonymizationFieldConfig records. Apex, the LWC, the four objects and all 39 of their
     fields, the four layouts, the tab, the permission set, the custom permission, the 14 shared
     pattern records and the org config record.

     WHY THE FIELD CONFIGS ARE EXCLUDED: they are what differs from one org to the next. They name
     objects, fields and record types that exist in one org and not another, and an org's admins
     edit them in Setup. Deploying them would overwrite that work and, worse, install configs
     pointing at objects the target org does not have — each one then silently skipped at run time,
     leaving the field it was meant to protect with its PII. Add or update field configs in their
     own deployment, deliberately.

     Members are generated from the repository tree, so nothing on disk is missed. Re-generate
     rather than hand-editing when files are added.

     BEFORE DEPLOYING, CHECK THAT NO RUN IS IN FLIGHT. A chained run holds a serialized
     Database.Stateful instance; redeploying the class it points at kills that run mid-chain, with
     the bypass left raised and the audit log stuck on Running:

       SELECT Id, Status, ApexClass.Name, CreatedDate FROM AsyncApexJob
       WHERE Status IN ('Queued','Processing','Preparing','Holding') AND ApexClass.Name LIKE 'TEKCO_%'

     UPGRADING FROM THE PRE-MERGE VERSION: the chain merge deleted five classes. They must go in
     the same deployment that installs their replacements, as a POST-destructive change:

       sf project deploy start ~-manifest <this file>
           ~-post-destructive-changes anonymization/manifest/destructiveChanges-architecture.xml
           ~-dry-run ~-target-org <alias>
     (replace ~- with double dashes; XML comments cannot contain them)

     NOT IN THIS MANIFEST, DELIBERATELY:

       - CXFCO_BypassCustomValidations / CXFCO_BypassOutboundSynchronization. A standard TEKCO org
         already owns these; they belong to the CXFCO application. The copies in this repository
         exist only so the permission set deploys to an org that lacks them (Portugal). Shipping
         them here would overwrite another application's definitions with ours.

       - CustomApplication Data_Anonymization. Its metadata names a utility bar,
         Data_Anonymization_UtilityBar, which is a FlexiPage that is NOT in this repository. The
         deployment fails in any org that does not already have it. A standard TEKCO org reaches
         the tool through an existing app (Run Teams Tools); add the tab there by hand.

       - TEKCO_AnonymizationFieldConfig records, per the note above.

     ABOUT TEKCO_AnonymizationOrgConfig.ALH_Portugal: it is the only org config record in the
     repository and it is Portugal's. In a TEKCO org it is inert, because getConfig() matches on
     the org domain prefix and this one names the Portugal sandbox's. It is included so the
     package stays a faithful copy of the project; drop the CustomMetadata block if you would
     rather not carry it.
-->
